WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.380
Rocks about 3.48 billion years old in the Dresser Formation of Western Australia

2
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.280
hold layered mounds.

3
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.840
A 2017 study read them as traces of life in hot springs.

4
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.660
So when did life begin?

5
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.300
These rocks cannot say.

6
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.540
They tell you that life existed by then.

7
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.340
Older traces could have been destroyed, never formed, or not yet found.

8
00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.153
Fossils are rarely dated directly.

9
00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:38.973
Minerals in the rocks around them are.

10
00:00:39.813 --> 00:00:42.993
Take a hypothetical zircon from volcanic ash.

11
00:00:43.673 --> 00:00:47.173
It took up uranium as it formed, but almost no lead.

12
00:00:48.053 --> 00:00:50.153
Its lead comes from later decay.

13
00:00:51.113 --> 00:00:53.293
So the mineral works like an hourglass.

14
00:00:53.973 --> 00:00:57.613
The sand in the bottom bulb tells you the time since it was turned over.

15
00:00:58.573 --> 00:01:02.213
The half-life is the time for half the parent atoms to decay.

16
00:01:02.213 --> 00:01:05.533
Here, it is 704 million years.

17
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:10.353
Now suppose the zircon has stayed closed since it formed.

18
00:01:11.093 --> 00:01:14.373
You measure three lead atoms for every uranium atom.

19
00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.753
Every lead atom was once a uranium atom.

20
00:01:17.793 --> 00:01:19.993
So the zircon started with four.

21
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:21.973
One quarter is left.

22
00:01:22.573 --> 00:01:23.953
That is two half-lives.

23
00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:29.233
Two times 704 is 1,408 million years.

24
00:01:30.053 --> 00:01:32.753
This is a model, only as good as its assumptions.

25
00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:35.777
Now date a fossil.

26
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:39.137
The ash lies above a fossil bed.

27
00:01:39.877 --> 00:01:45.097
A second ash, below the bed, is dated to 1,450 million years.

28
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:52.137
So the fossils are younger than 1,450 and older than 1,408 million years.

29
00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:55.157
The answer is a bracket, not a point.

30
00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:59.167
Each of these firsts is a minimum age.

31
00:02:00.007 --> 00:02:04.167
The oldest fossil sets a floor, and the lineage may be older.

32
00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:11.007
Preservation is uneven in space and time, so a gap in the record is not a gap in

33
00:02:11.007 --> 00:02:14.387
life. The bias works at the other end too.

34
00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:19.247
A species' last fossil usually lies below where it actually vanished.

35
00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.320
So read every date the same way.

36
00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:30.200
It has a measured age, a method, an uncertainty, and a direction in which the truth

37
00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:37.540
could lie. The Dresser rocks show that life existed by 3.48 billion years ago.

38
00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:43.660
The oldest fossil tells you when life existed by, never when it began.
